# YY Leathers - New Supabase Setup Guide

Your old Supabase project hit the free tier quota limit (exceed_cached_egress_quota). This guide walks you through setting up a new optimized Supabase project from scratch.

## Step 1: Create a New Supabase Project

1. Go to https://supabase.com and sign in
2. Click New Project
3. Fill in: Name, Database Password (save it!), Region (Mumbai ap-south-1), Plan (Free)
4. Wait 2-3 minutes for provisioning

## Step 2: Run the SQL Schema

1. In Supabase dashboard, go to SQL Editor
2. Open `app/supabase-schema.sql` from this project
3. Copy ALL content and paste into SQL editor
4. Click Run - should see "Success"

This creates: yy_store_sync table, profiles table, yy-images storage bucket, RLS policies, seed data, admin profile.

## Step 3: Get Your API Keys

1. In Supabase dashboard, go to Settings then API
2. Copy: Project URL, anon public key, service_role key (KEEP SECRET)

## Step 4: Update Your .env File

Open `app/.env` and replace OLD Supabase values with NEW ones:

```
VITE_SUPABASE_URL="https://YOUR_NEW_PROJECT.supabase.co"
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY="your_new_anon_key_here"
SUPABASE_URL="https://YOUR_NEW_PROJECT.supabase.co"
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY="your_new_anon_key_here"
```

## Step 5: Migrate Your Data

Run the migration script to copy all data from db.json to new Supabase:

PowerShell:
```
$env:SUPABASE_URL="https://YOUR_NEW_PROJECT.supabase.co"
$env:SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY="your_service_role_key_here"
cd app
node migrate-to-supabase.mjs
```

## Step 6: Re-upload Product Images (IMPORTANT)

Product images are on the OLD Supabase Storage (down due to quota). You must re-upload them:

Option A: Upload to new Supabase Storage bucket "yy-images" then update URLs in admin panel
Option B: Use Cloudinary (free 25GB) - upload images and update URLs
Option C: Use Imgur or another free image host

## Step 7: Enable Google OAuth

1. Supabase dashboard - Authentication - Providers - Enable Google
2. Add Google OAuth Client ID and Secret
3. Set redirect URL to your Supabase callback URL

## Step 8: Run the Website

```
cd app
npm run dev
```

Open http://localhost:3000

Testing Login (localhost only):
- Customer: Enter any email in the Localhost Testing Login section
- Admin: Click "Login as Admin (No Password)" button

## Step 9: Deploy to Netlify

Update Netlify env vars: VITE_SUPABASE_URL, VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY, SUPABASE_URL, SUPABASE_ANON_KEY

## Optimization Tips to Avoid Hitting Quota Again

What was optimized:
1. Removed hardcoded old credentials from supabase.ts
2. Increased cache TTL from 15 min to 30 min
3. Only fetches public data for regular visitors
4. Admin data fetched separately only when admin logs in

Best practices:
1. Use Cloudinary for images instead of Supabase Storage (images = #1 cause of egress quota)
2. Keep product descriptions short
3. Monitor usage in Supabase dashboard - Settings - Usage
4. Set up spending caps in Supabase
5. Use a CDN (Cloudflare) in front of your site

Free tier limits: 500MB DB, 1GB Storage, 5GB Bandwidth/month
Pro plan ($25/month): 8GB DB, 100GB Storage, 250GB Bandwidth/month

